                  ],
                  "description": "Typically, eclectic techniques model the relationship between the last hidden layer and the outputs, then infer the input-output relationship from the magnitudes of the weights in a NN. However, few of them are based on DTs. Therefore, this survey comprises approaches that extract partial knowledge contained in the hidden layers and do not demand their approximation target is the input-output relationship",
                  "node_type": "group",
                  "title": "1.2.3 Eclectic Techniques."
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "node_type": "group",
                      "title": "Tree regularization",
